                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "To all the pixel-loving freaks, this is just another dumb brawler mashup where you just button-mash your way into therapy. Atleast that's what I thought about this game during first impressions. I was like Nah, in this age of Chernobyl reactor powered AAA games, why the blocks am I even checking this game out. But the visuals are like a sugar-coated fever dream. Everything’s colorful, shiny, and slightly horny in that “I can’t look away” kinda way. I figured, “F*** it, I’ll give it a go on Steam — worst case, I uninstall it and go cry. The gameplay feels like My brain’s doing backflips, my hands are sweating, my controller’s probably filing for abuse. It’s manic, it’s messy, it’s absolutely beautiful. And when you play with friends? Oh baby Jesus in a leather jacket, it’s like a cocaine-fueled pillow fight in a Lego factory. Everyone’s screaming, blocks are flying, towers are exploding, and somehow you’re still having the time of your f***ing life. Whoever designed this must’ve mainlined rainbows and caffeine for a week straight. \nThis game is a tetris lifestyle where you need absolutely no basic knowledge of tetris to begin making sense out of this game and when you do, It makes your blood pressure skyrocket, your friendships crumble, and your dopamine levels explode like fireworks in your brain. \nWould absolutely destroy my friends again, screaming, “EAT MY BLOCKS!\"",
